# This file used to be a single `*`, which ignored the whole repository. Tracked
# files kept working, so nothing looked wrong -- but every new file was invisible
# to `git status` unless somebody remembered `git add -f`. LICENSE, the privacy
# document, and two test files had already been missed that way. A clone would
# have had no licence at all.
#
# So: name what must stay out, and let everything else be seen.

# Conversation logs. These must never enter a commit, and no fixture may be
# built from one -- a fixture made from a real transcript carries whatever the
# transcript carried.
*.jsonl

# The snapshot store. It holds keyed hashes of session ids, project names, and
# command tokens; committing it publishes them. `snapshot/stateDir.ts` refuses
# to run against a store that git tracks, and this is the other half of that.
snapshots/
.agent-eval/
.agent-eval-key
*.key

# A token-bearing .npmrc must never become a tracked file.
.npmrc

node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tgz
.env
.env.*
